course: dictionary
lesson: 14477
title: Pastime
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pastime is something you enjoy doing in your free time. It can be a hobby, a game or a sport. The word is a noun, so you can say a pastime or pastimes.
explain: «My favourite pastimes are drawing, swimming and reading.» These are things the writer enjoys doing when school is finished. To check, swap in the word hobby: «My favourite hobbies are drawing, swimming and reading.» It still makes sense, so hobby is close in meaning.
explain: Pastimes are not only for today. «Long ago, children played hopscotch, marbles and archery for fun.» In history lessons, these games are pastimes from the past, and you can find clues about them in the words around the word.
fact: A pastime is something you enjoy doing in your free time.
fact: A pastime can be a hobby, a game or a sport.
fact: «Hopscotch», «marbles» and «archery» were pastimes long ago.
fact: In England and the USA, cricket and baseball are called national pastimes.
exercise: «My favourite pastimes are drawing and cycling.» What is a pastime? | *Something you enjoy doing in your free time | A long journey to another town | A lesson you must do at school | A kind of food
exercise: Which of these was a pastime long ago? | Smartphone | Electric car | Email | *Hopscotch
exercise: Cricket and baseball are called what in England and the USA? | Winter clothes | School subjects | Lost games | *National pastimes
test: «Her pastime is painting pictures in the garden on Sunday.» Find and copy one word that means a hobby or activity you enjoy. | garden | Sunday | painting | *pastime
test: Which word is closest in meaning to pastime? | Chore | Journey | *Hobby | Homework
exam: Ravi says, «My pastime is archery.» What does the word pastime tell you about archery? | It is something Ravi enjoys doing in his free time | *It is a subject Ravi must study at school | It is a food Ravi likes | It is a place Ravi visits every day
